      "summary": "# Conversation Summary\n\n1. **Initial Request**: Make the GlobalSettings view responsive and mobile-friendly by converting the left sidebar to a collapsible drawer on mobile with icon-only buttons.\n\n2. **First Implementation**: Created a responsive layout using Tailwind's `md:` breakpoints with a desktop sidebar and mobile drawer navigation that auto-closes when tabs are selected.\n\n3. **Container Query Adjustment**: Updated the implementation to use Tailwind's `@md:` and `@sm:` container query selectors instead of viewport breakpoints since the component renders in a resizable desktop panel.\n\n4. **Final Solution**: Delivered a fully responsive GlobalSettings view that dynamically adapts to panel width, hiding the sidebar and showing a drawer on narrow containers while maintaining full functionality.\n\n5. **Key Features**: Icon-only mobile buttons, smooth transitions between layouts, proper spacing adjustments, and persistent state management across different screen sizes.",
